    <!-- Help / How to download guide -->
    <string name="help_title">How to download videos</string>
    <string name="help_subtitle">Three quick steps to grab any video you can play in the browser.</string>
    <string name="help_step1_title">1. Open the video page</string>
    <string name="help_step1_body">Tap a tile on the home screen, or type any URL in the search bar at the top. SuperX opens the page in its built-in browser the same way Chrome would.</string>
    <string name="help_step2_title">2. Press play and wait for detection</string>
    <string name="help_step2_body">Hit the play button on the video. SuperX watches the network in the background and the floating button shows a loading animation while it scans for every available quality. This usually takes 5–50 seconds depending on the site.</string>
    <string name="help_step3_title">3. Tap the download button and choose a quality</string>
    <string name="help_step3_body">Once the loading dots stop, the floating download button turns solid. Tap it, pick the resolution you want from the dialog, then press the colored Download button. Your file moves to the Progress tab and lands in Finished when it is done.</string>
    <string name="help_tip_title">Helpful tips</string>
    <string name="help_tip_body">• If a video is not detected, tap reload on the page or switch the site to Desktop mode from the menu.\n• Some sites stream multi-part files. The download will keep going in the background even if you close the page.\n• You can change the ad-detection threshold and thread count in Settings under General.\n• Long-press a tile on the home screen to remove it from your favorites.</string>
